## Summary

Implements the first Laravel/MariaDB slice of **GF-FR-005 Distribution**.

### Distribution core
- adds tenant-owned `publication_deliveries`, unique per schedule;
- persists a stable provider idempotency key across every retry;
- adds a provider contract/registry with no real platform adapters enabled;
- distinguishes authentication, rate-limit and transient failures;
- persists attempts, retry time, claim lease and safe error codes;
- bounds provider attempts at four;
- redrives abandoned queued/processing work after a five-minute lease;
- revalidates actor, tenant, schedule, destination and current media-processing eligibility immediately before provider I/O;
- filters terminal/leased delivery history before the scheduler batch limit to prevent starvation;
- treats already-published delivery as a no-op.

### Retry semantics
- authentication failure is terminal;
- rate limits schedule a bounded 60-3600 second retry;
- transient failures use persisted backoff;
- successful retries reuse the exact same idempotency key and cannot create a second GrindFlow delivery row.

### Runtime
Adds `grindflow:dispatch-publications` to the Laravel scheduler every minute. The tick is deploy-before-migration safe and returns zero work until `publication_deliveries` exists.

### Safety
This PR does **not** apply migrations, enable real providers, use provider credentials, rotate secrets, or publish external content.

### Required validation
Selected gates:
`preflight · fast[contracts] · php-quality · PHPUnit · MariaDB · browser`.

Legacy is intentionally out of scope for this diff.

